<!--
      Internet relays (the spool plane, docs/SPOOL_PROTOCOL.md).

      Two rules hold this copy together. First, a relay refusal is never a failed send: the mesh still
      carries the message, so every string here talks about *reach* ("nearby only", "not covered")
      rather than failure. Second, the disclosure is deliberately concrete about what a relay observes
      — vague reassurance would be the dishonest option for a feature that ships sealed bytes to a
      machine the user does not hold.
    -->
